# T0051 — Shared list view, wired to ToDo lists

**Task:** T0051 (id 51) · **Branch (on approval):** `T0051-todo-list-view`  
**State at plan:** `ready` · no Depends-on blockers

## Goal

Extract a reusable list-view component (column header, column sort, personalize, drag reorder) and use it on **ToDo lists**. Task project boards and the global Tasks page stay as they are. Ideas move onto the same component in follow-up **T0157** (Draft, depends on T0051).

## Interview decisions (locked)

| # | Decision |
|---|----------|
| 1 | Shared component, **ToDo lists first**. Ideas are T0157. |
| 2 | **Groups skipped** (project task groups are not a ToDo concept). |
| 3 | **Manual order is default.** Drag persists `todo_list_items.sort_order`. While manual order is active, no column sort is active. Choosing a column sort leaves manual order until the user returns to it. |
| 4 | Folding skipped. ToDo membership is a flat list (no parent tree on the list). |
| 5 | Existing ToDo clause filter stays. Drag is disabled while a filter is active so hidden rows are not reordered. |

The old pause paragraph in the T0051 description (Ideas stay separate; ToDo already has its own features) is superseded by this split.

## Out of scope

- Rewriting `TaskBoard` or `TasksListPage` onto the new component.
- Ideas list (`IdeasListPage`) — **T0157**.
- Task groups, group drag, parent/child folding.
- Unifying the task filter engine with the ToDo filter engine.
- Inbox / Unsorted lists: order stays virtual (API already rejects persisting that order). Column sort may still apply client-side; drag stays disabled.

